{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And behold, a great dark terror fell upon him.</b> There is hinted to him here the subjugation of the four kingdoms, as the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: 'terror' — this is Babylon; 'darkness' — this is Media, for they darkened the eyes of Israel with fasting and affliction; 'great' — this is Greece; 'falling upon him' — this is Edom." "<b>And the Ramban</b> of blessed memory <b>wrote:</b> the prophet found in his soul <b>terror</b>, and afterward it came into <b>darkness</b>, and afterward the darkness <b>grew great</b>, and afterward he felt as though it were <b>falling upon him</b>. And this matter was for Abraham, for when the Holy One, blessed be He, cut a covenant with him to give the land to his seed as an everlasting possession, He told him, as it were, by way of reservation in His gift, that four kingdoms would subjugate his children and rule over their land — and this on condition if they sin before Him. And afterward He informed him in explanation of another exile that they would undergo first — this is the exile of Egypt, for which he had already been punished. Thus far."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:36.191520136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}